    "knowledge_point": "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation",
    "problem": "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sqrt{t+9},\\,\\,\\,y=t+1,\\,t\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$",
    "worked_solution": "To find the range of $x,$ note that $\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 3$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Consequently, $x=2\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 6.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude that $x\\ge 6.$",
